{
  "decision": "add_family",
  "rationale": "The iterative and unrolled_k families are fundamentally infeasible for this spec because they cannot meet the throughput constraint. The best throughput observed for iterative is 11.7 MSPS and for unrolled_k is 10.3 MSPS, both well below the required 32 MSPS. Furthermore, the system latency constraint (sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44 us) is violated by over 500% for the best designs in these families, as they take multiple cycles to process a single request. The pipelined and pipelined_m families are the only ones that produce one result per cycle, which is necessary to achieve the 32 MSPS throughput and the tight 0.44 us batch latency. I will add these families to the search space.",
